{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/53011-majesty-questions","id":53011,"title":"Majesty Questions?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-01-18T22:13:15-08:00","id":53011,"title":"Majesty Questions?","content":"Just some questions about how Majesty feels. Is it particular to a character? Can they control the sort of mojo they're putting out there? How does it feel as a character to activate Awe?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-08T15:37:51-07:00","id":473437,"title":"","content":"My question is in regards to Awe and it's effects on humans. As an example, the fluff describes a vampire killing a human being in public (beating them to death) and no one minding (no social penalties, etc.) Though naturally they'd have even more witnesses now that's a problem for later. So would that mean they could shoot a cop surrounded by cops and walk away with high fives? That seems pretty potent for the first dot of an incontestable discipline.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My horror roleplaying blog with a strong focus on World of Darkness and Call of Cthulhu can be found here: <a href=\"http://stwildonroleplaying.blogspot.com.au/\" target=\"_blank\">http://stwildonroleplaying.blogspot.com.au/</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1248-laraqua","name":"Laraqua","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"107"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-08T15:52:55-07:00","id":473462,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Laraqua</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/53011-majesty-questions?p=473437#post473437\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My question is in regards to Awe and it's effects on humans. As an example, the fluff describes a vampire killing a human being in public (beating them to death) and no one minding (no social penalties, etc.) Though naturally they'd have even more witnesses now that's a problem for later. So would that mean they could shoot a cop surrounded by cops and walk away with high fives? That seems pretty potent for the first dot of an incontestable discipline.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's a huge difference between &quot;no penalties to social rolls&quot; and &quot;no one minds&quot;. If you shoot a cop, you'll have trouble on your hands no matter what. But thanks to awe, you'll have a much easier time convincing the other cops to go easier on you thanks to the lack of dice penalties. You're still getting arrested though, because damn.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-08T16:11:53-07:00","id":473479,"title":"","content":"Basically a good way to look at it is, people affected by Awe will always interpret thing in the most positive fashion regarding you... but, y'know, even the best spin doctors would have trouble with making a cop-killer look good.<br /> <br /> <b>Edit</b>: To give more examples of what I mean:<br /> <br /> You are not creepy. You are awkward in that cute, adorable way.<br /> You are not aggressive and dangerous. You are hot-blooded.<br /> You are not a ticking time bomb. You just had a bad day.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Politeness is the lubricant of social intercourse.","edited":{"userid":272,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/272-saibot","user":"saibot","date":". 04-08-2015, 07:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/272-saibot","name":"saibot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1063"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-11T12:02:39-07:00","id":477155,"title":"","content":"I think with the cop-shooting scenario, you could probably use Awe to not get shot, so the cops around you are more likely to use non-lethal takedowns, to assume you had a decent reason for doing what you did, more likely to cut you a deal, that kinda thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2291-gwyn-chan-r-gwyll","name":"Gwyn chan 'r Gwyll","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}